Why?

1337
01:15:00,480 --> 01:15:01,600
Stop being on target.

1338
01:15:02,780 --> 01:15:03,760
I didn't change that.

1339
01:15:03,800 --> 01:15:04,680
That's so weird that it did that.

1340
01:15:07,780 --> 01:15:08,580
Here we go.

1341
01:15:18,700 --> 01:15:19,620
Look at that.

1342
01:15:21,140 --> 01:15:21,860
That's pretty.

1343
01:15:22,460 --> 01:15:24,780
And now we're gonna run one of these bad boys.

1344
01:15:25,760 --> 01:15:27,560
Seismic data from the greater flats.

1345
01:15:28,220 --> 01:15:30,060
Faint seismic waves are detected.

1346
01:15:31,020 --> 01:15:31,560
Okay.

1347
01:15:32,200 --> 01:15:33,040
Toggle display.

1348
01:15:34,460 --> 01:15:35,020
Wow.

1349
01:15:35,200 --> 01:15:36,420
0.05G.

1350
01:15:37,180 --> 01:15:38,600
That is very little.

1351
01:15:40,420 --> 01:15:42,580
Like, jumping here is a serious flight risk.

1352
01:15:45,100 --> 01:15:47,060
Okay, so we gotta go out there and collect that now.

1353
01:15:48,880 --> 01:15:49,640
Take data.

1354
01:15:50,740 --> 01:15:51,620
EVA report.

1355
01:15:51,920 --> 01:15:52,760
Nothing there.

1356
01:15:53,340 --> 01:15:54,540
But let me try...

1357
01:15:54,540 --> 01:15:56,140
...to do a little bit of...

1358
01:15:58,300 --> 01:15:58,740
...whatchamacallit.

1359
01:15:58,880 --> 01:15:59,580
...surface sample.

1360
01:16:00,440 --> 01:16:02,380
Don't know if I've done that on these flats yet.

1361
01:16:03,540 --> 01:16:05,360
That's a recent thing we have gotten here.

1362
01:16:06,620 --> 01:16:07,960
Yeah, look at that, man!

1363
01:16:07,960 --> 01:16:09,000
0.45G!

1364
01:16:09,000 --> 01:16:11,580
You sneak a taste of the surface sample.

1365
01:16:12,020 --> 01:16:12,240
Nope.

1366
01:16:12,520 --> 01:16:15,140
It definitely is not made of delicious dessert products.

1367
01:16:18,640 --> 01:16:19,200
Christ.

1368
01:16:20,640 --> 01:16:21,540
Another flag?

1369
01:16:21,680 --> 01:16:21,780
Nah.

1370
01:16:22,000 --> 01:16:22,940
One flag is enough, right?

1371
01:16:23,420 --> 01:16:24,480
Actually, let's do one more.

1372
01:16:27,640 --> 01:16:30,020
We're gonna document what Nilden has done here.

1373
01:16:34,470 --> 01:16:37,450
This is called Nilden's Shame.

1374
01:16:37,450 --> 01:16:55,390
This is where Nilden decided to put the surface samples in his mouth, thereby contaminating the science.

1375
01:16:56,930 --> 01:16:57,470
Boo!

1376
01:16:58,270 --> 01:16:59,570
Bad Nilden.

1377
01:17:01,090 --> 01:17:01,970
There we go.

1378
01:17:06,900 --> 01:17:07,280
Okay.

1379
01:17:08,140 --> 01:17:08,860
In we go.

1380
01:17:11,400 --> 01:17:12,440
And now we gotta...

1381
01:17:14,440 --> 01:17:15,720
I guess we just go home, man.

1382
01:17:15,980 --> 01:17:16,520
I mean...

1383
01:17:16,520 --> 01:17:17,720
We have so much fuel left, dude!

1384
01:17:17,900 --> 01:17:18,600
Should we do something else?

1385
01:17:18,880 --> 01:17:19,380
Hold on.

1386
01:17:19,480 --> 01:17:20,500
Let me see my quests.

1387
01:17:21,600 --> 01:17:22,220
Plant flag.

1388
01:17:22,860 --> 01:17:24,980
Transmit or recover scientific data from space around memes.

1389
01:17:25,100 --> 01:17:26,080
We did that one, pretty much.

1390
01:17:26,240 --> 01:17:26,700
That's done.

1391
01:17:29,220 --> 01:17:30,440
We saved both people.

1392
01:17:30,680 --> 01:17:31,720
That's incredible.

1393
01:17:31,720 --> 01:17:31,840
Incredible.

1394
01:17:34,380 --> 01:17:35,140
I think...

1395
01:17:35,140 --> 01:17:36,240
We're good, man.

1396
01:17:37,460 --> 01:17:40,840
Maybe we take some more Magneto-Meto-Boom reports on the way home, but that's about it.

1397
01:17:46,100 --> 01:17:46,840
That's about it.

1398
01:17:51,950 --> 01:17:52,710
Now we wait.

1399
