Oh, wait!

1405
01:18:19,440 --> 01:18:20,140
I have it on target!

1406
01:18:20,820 --> 01:18:22,080
Why does it keep changing?

1407
01:18:24,700 --> 01:18:27,620
I mean, not that it would change anything, I don't think, but still, that's annoying.

1408
01:18:28,460 --> 01:18:29,480
It keeps switching.

1409
01:18:37,490 --> 01:18:39,090
Oh my god, did I really just do that?

1410
01:18:39,250 --> 01:18:39,570
Jesus.

1411
01:18:41,270 --> 01:18:42,130
Well, you know what?

1412
01:18:43,710 --> 01:18:44,730
Let's just keep burning.

1413
01:18:45,390 --> 01:18:46,090
There we go.

1414
01:18:46,370 --> 01:18:46,730
Escape.

1415
01:18:47,610 --> 01:18:48,170
Fuck it.

1416
01:18:48,930 --> 01:18:50,650
We don't need to be efficient right now.

1417
01:18:51,270 --> 01:18:52,610
Okay, so we're in space right now.

1418
01:18:52,610 --> 01:18:54,210
I need to check the magnetometer.

1419
01:18:56,170 --> 01:18:57,090
Run the test.

1420
01:18:59,170 --> 01:19:00,590
I love the animation of this.

1421
01:19:00,730 --> 01:19:01,070
It's cool.

1422
01:19:03,810 --> 01:19:10,970
In space, high over Minmus, you've measured the interaction between the solar wind and the magnetic field of this body as it deflects charged particles.

1423
01:19:11,390 --> 01:19:14,290
So this also has a magnetic field.

1424
01:19:14,430 --> 01:19:15,070
What the fuck?

1425
01:19:16,510 --> 01:19:17,870
It looks dead, man.

1426
01:19:18,990 --> 01:19:20,230
What is causing that?

